/-
NagataHigman/Paper/Statements.lean — one theorem per claim of the paper
"Improving Razmyslov's (1974) bound: the Nagata–Higman index is at most n^2-2 for n >= 3" (Dave Goel, short v1.03); "line" = line of
its LaTeX source.
Bodies link to proofs elsewhere; an unproved body = NOT proved yet (the audit marks it OPEN).
Author: Dave Goel. Copyright (C) Dave Goel 2026--now.

Indexing (see the Defs files): letters x_0, x_1, … (paper x_1, x_2, …); S_N acts on {0, …, N-1} (paper {1, …, N});
tableau entries 0, …, N-1; cells (row, column) 0-indexed. Paper symbols vs Lean names: in Proposition 2.1 the set K,
the first-return map τ̄, the points w and the cycles θ are `X`, `s`, `x` and `ρ`; the corners a₊, a₋ of ν are the cells
`(n-2, n-1)`, `(n-1, n-2)`; Q± = (1 ± Y_N)/2 are `projPlus`, `projMinus`; the operator D of Lemma 4.2 is `stepD`; the
algebra 𝒴 generated by the Y_j is `Algebra.adjoin F (Set.range fun j => ρ(X^{(j)}))`. Every claim that involves the
representations of S_N is stated for an ARBITRARY Young system `Y` (Defs/YoungSystem.lean; one exists by
Cited/Classical.lean), so it holds in particular for Young's seminormal form, whose `Y.block λ` is the paper's isotypic
block I_λ. Section 4's claims that the paper makes over ℂ (line 396) take `Y : YoungSystem ℂ N`. The three (T3) claims
on Γ over ℂ also take the cited splitting of their one shape `λ` as a hypothesis (Defs/AlternatingSplit.lean):
`Gamma_support` the splitting with Frobenius' clause (`AltSplit`), `Gamma_pm` and `Gamma_trace_even` the splitting
alone (`AltDecomp`). Corollary 1.1 (Defs/MatrixInvariants.lean) is stated last: its proof uses Theorem B.
-/
